 <item
  id="60"
  ean=""
  name="Commander Keen 1: MArooned on Mars"
  boxpic=""
  backpic=""
  platform=""
  players="Offline: 1"
  editor="Apogee Software, Ltd."
  developer="id Software, Inc."
  released="1990"
  web="http://www.mobygames.com/game/dos/commander-keen-1-marooned-on-mars##MobyGames"
  rating="0"
  ratingpress="0"
  case="1"
  manual="1"
  exclusive="0"
  added="05/05/2015"
  completion="0"
  resolutions=""
  location=""
  installationsize="0"
  installationsizeunit="0"
  executable=""
  screenshot1=""
  screenshot2=""
  code=""
  unlockable=""
  region=""
  serialnumber=""
  borrower="none"
  lendDate=""
  borrowings=""
  favourite="0"
  tags=""
 >
  <description>Billy &quot;Commander Keen&quot; Blaze, an eight-year-old genius, has flied to Mars in his Bean-with-Bacon Megarocket build out of common household objects. But while Keen was exploring Mars, the alien Vorticons stole vital parts from his ship and hid them in the Martian cities. Now Keen must find the stolen parts if he wants to return to Earth.

Commander Keen 1: Marooned on Mars is the first in a series of platform games. Your objective is to find the 4 missing parts to your ship.

The game begins with a top-down map of Mars. This is the level select screen, where you can walk around and choose the next level you want to enter. On each level, you have to find the exit, and possibly grab a missing rocket part which may be on the level. Once you reach the exit, you're back on the map of Mars.

The levels are typically full of enemy creatures. Most numerous are Yorps, which are mostly harmless, if annoying, but other creatures are a genuine danger. If Keen gets shot or touched, or falls into a pit or some hazardous object, he dies, and you're booted out of the level back to the map of Mars and lose one of the lives.

Thankfully, Keen can defeat some of the enemies with his raygun. He can also find a pogo stick which allows him to jump very high. Other items to find include keycards that open locked doors and bonus items which give score (Keen gets an extra life if he collects enough score).</description>
  <comments></comments>
  <secrets>All keys and pogo stick!

While playing, Press Ctrl, Tab and Space simultaneously.





God mode.
While playing, press G, O, and D simultaneously.





Pogo Shrine
Once you get the pogo, activate it, and pogo up and to the right off of the silver cylinders. There are hidden bricks that you may jump on to get to a higher place in the level.

(Taken from the official hint booklet supplied with the retail version on the game.)


Ice City
To get past the Vorticon without firing, let him jump on the blue cylinders and then run underneath him.

(Taken from the official hint booklet supplied with the retail version on the game.)


Vorticon Commander's Castle
There are hidden bricks in the entrance hallway that lead to bonus points!

(Taken from the official hint booklet supplied with the retail version on the game.)


How to find the secret base
Go to the Dark Side of the Mars, once you are there, go to the gray mars base in the centre of Mars. Enter it. Play the level normally. Once you reached the red keycard, you have jumped over a chasm with fire. That's the way to the secret base. Jump down, but avoid the flames on the bottom, which are direct beneath the route you fall. If you survived, take the right way, there is a big wall. You can't jump high enough, even with the pogo, to cross it. But you can see a spot on the wall of the chasm, there you must go with the pogo. Now jump over the wall, but be careful not to fall into the freezing machine. If so, you will be frozen and than land in the fire and die. Jump over the fire, stand directly left of the wall, jump with the pogo directly into the freezing ball on the point of the cannons maximal fire distance. If you do it correct, you will be catapulted over the wall. Once you landed, use the ray of the robot to thaw yourself, now you are ready to jump into the teleporter. When you done this, you are back on Mars' worldmap, far east beyond the mountain east of the gray base you started. Now you can play the secret base...</secrets>
  <genre>
   <line>
    <col>Action</col>
   </line>
   <line>
    <col>Action/Platform</col>
   </line>
  </genre>
 </item>
 <item
  id="61"
  ean=""
  name="Cosmo's Cosmic Adventures"
  boxpic=""
  backpic=""
  platform=""
  players="1"
  editor="Apogee Software, Ltd."
  developer="Apogee Software, Ltd."
  released="1992"
  web="http://www.mobygames.com/game/dos/cosmos-cosmic-adventure-forbidden-planet##MobyGames"
  rating="0"
  ratingpress="0"
  case="1"
  manual="1"
  exclusive="0"
  added="05/05/2015"
  completion="0"
  resolutions=""
  location=""
  installationsize="0"
  installationsizeunit="0"
  executable=""
  screenshot1=""
  screenshot2=""
  unlockable=""
  region=""
  serialnumber=""
  borrower="none"
  lendDate=""
  borrowings=""
  favourite="0"
  tags=""
 >
  <description>On a trip with his parents to every kid's favorite place in the universe (Disney World, of course), Cosmo becomes stranded on a planet, his parents vanished.  You direct him as he runs and jumps through different lands, such as alien tropics, haunted forest, ice cave, and future world, to find his parents.  Along the way he encounters the various platform baddies that he must either jump to death in the classic style or destroy with bombs.  Bombs are also useful for finding secrets.  Cosmo is also armed with suction cup arms which he can use to climb up tall walls.</description>
  <comments></comments>
  <secrets>Falling Stars

When you're on high platforms, look up to cause stars and other bonuses to possibly fall from above.  Collect enough stars and you can visit bonus levels.



Special invincibility

Give &quot;apogee&quot; on the command line when starting up Cosmo. 
The effects of this are many. One, the game will not recognize 
your old high scores or saved games. (The high scores will be reset to 
those of Simpsons' characters until you exit and re-enter the program 
normally.) In this mode, if you die quickly enough after entering 
a level, you'll be invincible from then on, to everything but pits on the 
bottom of each level. 




Source: &lt;a href=&quot;/search/quick?company=Apogee&quot;&gt;Apogee&lt;/a&gt;'s Official Website - &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.apogee1.com&quot;&gt;http://www.apogee1.com&lt;/a&gt;


See Duke and Get a Sandwich
In the seventh level of this game's second chapter, if you fall through a set of transparent set of bricks fairly close to the beginning of the level, you will end up in a secret tunnel below the level. Follow this tunnel to its end, and you will find a frozen Duke Nukem. Lay a bomb at his feet, and he'll become defrosted. After a brief dialog, he'll fly away to save the galaxy and give you a Sandwich that extends your life meter by one full slot!</secrets>
  <genre>
   <line>
    <col>Action</col>
   </line>
   <line>
    <col>Action/Platform</col>
   </line>
  </genre>
  <code>
   <line>
    <col>Pressing [C] [0] [F10] down simultaneously will give you a full health and bombs. This cheat only works once per game. Debug Mode:Pressing [tab] [del] [F12] at once activates debug mode. The debug keys are: [F10] [G] - God mode [F10] [W] - Warp [F10] [M] - Display memory usage statistics Source: &lt;a href=&quot;/search/quick?company=Apogee&quot;&gt;Apogee&lt;/a&gt;'s Official Website - &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.apogee1.com&quot;&gt;http://www.apogee1.com&lt;/a&gt;</col>
    <col>Official Cheat Codes and Debug Mode</col>
   </line>
  </code>
 </item>
