  serialnumber=""
  borrower="none"
  lendDate=""
  borrowings=""
  favourite="0"
  tags=""
 >
  <description>In his second adventure James Pond must retrieve the toys Dr Maybe has stolen. Pond has been armed with an Inspector Gadget-style stretch device, which he can use to view higher areas or claw onto ceilings so as to slide across them.

The gameplay takes place across worlds themed around particular types of toys, such as sporting goods, candy and aircraft. The levels scroll sideways, although a small amount of vertical movement is included. On each level Pond must collect 2 penguins and reach the exit, although there are usually multiple exits and lots of secret areas to explore. After completing each pair of two worlds (each of which has three sub levels), a boss must be faced.</description>
  <comments></comments>
  <secrets>KIll the Teddy Bear-boss EASY
Jump and duck at the same time on his head and the boss will die after 5-9 times doing this little trick!


Invincibility
When you start the game move right until you notice a number of pickups on the roof above you. Collect them in the following order:

Cake
Heart
Earth
Apple
Tap

You will gain invincibility and all levels will be opened. Although not infinite, the invincibility lasts considerably longer than that provided from pickups within the game.</secrets>
  <genre>
   <line>
    <col>Action</col>
   </line>
   <line>
    <col>Action/Platform</col>
   </line>
  </genre>
  <code>
   <line>
    <col>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Behind the main tower are two hidden worlds, another Sweetslevel (including a Liquorice Allsorts World, the infamous BouncingJelly World, another Cake World and an upside down Jelly World), and an extra scrolling section. To reach them, have Robocod run along the ground floor, while avoiding the doors, then go up and over the first flight of stairs. From the bottom of the second tower, make your way up to the landing located above Dr. Maybe's final door and run left into the wall. You will disappear behind the screen and arrive in the Secret Tower room. But who is Katie?&lt;li&gt;Once you have finished the Bath level, drop down to the bottom of the castle, and walk left until you reach the small snowman statues. Jumping on these statues will cause them to turn into a moving platform. Once you get to the top of the screen, walk left into thin air and jump.  By now, you should be next to some doors.  Go through them to arrive at the bonus city.&lt;li&gt;Go to the same place after finishing the Circus room (the last room before the end of game baddy) and stand on the golden snowmen again. A platform made of two bonud blocks should float upwards, revealing a secret tunnel.  At the end of this are even more extra lives and stars.&lt;li&gt;Do as above after the Sweets level, but go to the left of thecastle.  Go on the snowmen once more, and at the top of the screen, get the umbrella and collect all the goodies while you floating down.&lt;li&gt;On the second Teddy Bear level, jump over the spikes repeatedly until you see a hole above you.  Jump through this hole and catapult yourself off the bus there. Once you have done this, get on the higher level and keep walking left, bounce on the trampoline and collect the wings.  Now fly along the top of the screen to the right and you should find a different exit.  Go through this for a special bonus level.&lt;li&gt;Complete a level that does not feature a guardian, and you willalways find something new when you return to the castle &quot;selection&quot; screen.  In one case you will find a whole sequence of elevators and shit that lead to a door that you cannot normally getto. In the Factory scene, go all the way right and look down. You will see a load of crowns, which you can access after comingback from other levels.&lt;li&gt;It is possible to finish &lt;i&gt;Robocod&lt;/i&gt; without completing all the levels.  A choice of two new doors to enter is given when the correct level is completed. Start by completing the Fluffy Toys one and then by doing the Cars one.&lt;li&gt;Finish the Bath levels and as soon as you come out of the door, run straight to the golden snowmen in the bottom far left outside the castle.  Jump into these snowmen and you'll float upwards to the top of the screen where you'll be met by a door.  Getting through this door is tricky but worth it.  Inside are loads of extra lives and energy stars.  Head for the same place after finishing the Crcus room (the last room before the end of game baddy) and stand on the golden snowmen again.  A platform made of two bonus blocks should float upwards revealing a secret tunnel.  At the end of this are even more extra lives and stars.</col>
    <col>Secret Room Locations</col>
   </line>
  </code>
 </item>
