  favourite="0"
  tags=""
 >
  <description>One year after the events described in The Colonel's Bequest, Laura Bow, fresh out of college, is hired by a New York newspaper to write a story about the newest exhibit acquired by the local Leyendecker Museum, an ancient Egyptian dagger. However, during a party to celebrate the opening of the museum's new section, someone is murdered, the dagger is stolen, and Laura, after asking to be allowed to investigate, is locked in with the rest of the guests. This sets the stage for a series of murders, and it is up to Laura to find the person responsible for them.

The Dagger of Amon Ra plays similarly to the The Colonel's Bequest, focusing primarily on exploration and clue-gathering rather than on solving puzzles, although there are more instances of inventory item collection and usage in the sequel. With the exception of the introductory act, the entire game is set in the museum. The player navigates Laura through its rooms and interacts with characters to gather information and uncover their true motives. The game's clock advances when it is triggered by certain actions or simply by moving from location to location. Some information and events may only be available in specific places and at specific times. Near the end of the game Laura will be asked to make a case to to the coroner, which involves answering a series of questions concerning the crimes. Depending on his playing style, clues discovered, and deductive skills, the player may or may not have the correct answers to all the questions.

Unlike its predecessor - and like most other contemporary Sierra adventures - the game utilizes an icon-based interface instead of typing verb-object commands to interact with the environments. Topics can also be chosen from a list when the player selects the &quot;Ask&quot; command. The CD version features full speech, including narration.</description>
  <comments></comments>
  <secrets>Solving audio and timing problems
&lt;i&gt;The Dagger of Amon Ra&lt;/i&gt; suffers from a few known bugs. The most common problems and their solutions:
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;On Soundblaster 16 cards, the game freezes after the first sound effect. Apply the official patch to solve the problem.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;The taxi rides never end / The safe in Carrington’s office doesn’t open. Both issues are timing problems that occur on modern PCs. There is an unofficial script patch that addresses both bugs. The alternative solution is to slow your computer down. If you’re playing the game under Windows, try using a slowdown tool. If you’re using &lt;a href=&quot;http://dosbox.sourceforge.net&quot;&gt;DOSBox&lt;/a&gt; for emulation (which is highly recommended), lower the CPU cycles (default key: F11) until the problems cease to occur.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
A site with all required downloads can be found in the related links section.

&lt;small&gt;Contributed by &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mobygames.com/user/sheet/userSheetId,1992/&quot;&gt;-Chris&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/small&gt;


Act 1: Laura Bow - A Nose for News
The Dagger of Amon Ra 

Walkthrough by *Katakis* (&lt;a class=&quot;__cf_email__&quot; href=&quot;/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection&quot; data-cfemail=&quot;3f5d5354485053590f0e7f58525e5653115c5052&quot;&gt;[email protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;script cf-hash='f9e31' type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
/* &lt;![CDATA[ */!function(){try{var t=&quot;currentScript&quot;in document?document.currentScript:function(){for(var t=document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;script&quot;),e=t.length;e--;)if(t[e].getAttribute(&quot;cf-hash&quot;))return t[e]}();if(t&amp;&amp;t.previousSibling){var e,r,n,i,c=t.previousSibling,a=c.getAttribute(&quot;data-cfemail&quot;);if(a){for(e=&quot;&quot;,r=parseInt(a.substr(0,2),16),n=2;a.length-n;n+=2)i=parseInt(a.substr(n,2),16)^r,e+=String.fromCharCode(i);e=document.createTextNode(e),c.parentNode.replaceChild(e,c)}}}catch(u){}}();/* ]]&gt; */&lt;/script&gt;)

You are Laura Bow, a post-graduate from Tulane University. After spending a night at the Dijon estate, you say goodbye to your parents and head to New York, where you are hired by the &lt;i&gt;Daily Register News Tribune&lt;/i&gt; to report on the theft of a priceless Egyptian artifact at the Leyendecker Museum. 

&lt;hr&gt;
* ACT 1 – Laura Bow: A Nose for News
&lt;hr&gt;

Laura is introduced to her assistant, Crodfoller T. Rhubarb, who has started investigating the case before her. You have a notebook and pencil in inventory. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

In the floppy version of &lt;i&gt;The Dagger of Amon Ra&lt;/i&gt;, Rhubarb tests your knowledge on Egyptology to prove that Laura is worthy of taking over the case. You are presented with a question and twelve symbols to choose from. In order to continue the game, you must pick out the correct symbol according to your game's documentation. If you choose an incorrect symbol, Laura is given the pink slip and the game will end.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Search the wastepaper basket and get the baseball inside. Bring a close-up of your desk by clicking the hand cursor on it, and lift the bottom-right corner of the blotter. Get the key and use it on the desk drawer. Get the press pass and close the drawer. Now, leave the close-up view and look around the office. 

Look at the bulletin board next to the Gents' lounge. Ask Rhubarb about the burglary. Rhub says that he was planning to talk to Ziggy who hangs out at the speakeasy.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

1. To ask people about something, click the talk cursor (with the question mark inside) on them to make Laura's notebook appear on screen. There are four tabs that appear on the side. Select the tab that you want, then click the subject in question. Now, right-click the mouse button until it changes to the exit cursor, then click the left-mouse button.
2. There are lots of topics that you can ask people about. You'll never know what you might learn from them. Also, by picking up objects, they can be asked about.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave the building and click the eye cursor on the street to make sure that it is safe to cross, then click on the yellow arrow to cross the street and end up at the police station. Look around. Examine the bum then enter the building. Now, examine the notices on the pillar and talk to the desk sergeant. He states that he needs food and tells Laura to go away. Knock on O'Riley's office door and enter. Laura will talk to O'Riley for quite a bit, and shown the file, which is a one-page summary detailing the theft of the Dagger of Amon Ra at the Leyendecker museum. After Laura tells him that the report is vague, O'Riley gets mad and throws Laura out of his office. Exit the police station. There is a newspaper lying on the ground where that bum was. Take the newspaper to discover a coupon. Get it. It's for a free sandwich from Luigi. Click the hand cursor on the yellow taxi sign to make Laura call for a taxi.

Say hello to Rocko, your taxi driver. He says that he can take you to any place if you have some cash or you are a member of the press. Sounds good. Since we don't have any cash, you must show him your press pass. When Rocko asks you where you like to be “motivated”, your notebook appears on screen. Click on the Places tab to bring up a list of locations you can visit, and choose to go to Lo Fat's Laundry.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

1. Make sure Laura has her press pass. You won't be going anywhere without it. 

2. Although the Leyendecker Museum is among the list of available locations, the main doors are locked until much later in the act.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Look at the three kids toasting ants with a magnifying glass, then talk to them. Give them the baseball and Laura will get the magnifying glass. Now, enter Lo Fat's and look at the evening gown behind him. Talk to Lo Fat. If you ask him about the Leyendecker Museum, he will tell you about the people who work there, namely Wolf Heimlich, Olympia Myklos, and Yvette Delacroix. Leave Lo Fat's and take a taxi back to the Trib.   

When you get out of the taxi, you see Luigi selling corn beef sandwiches. Talk to him, then give him the coupon. Take the sandwich back to the desk sergeant at the police station, then you can ask him about Yvette, Ziggy, and the Speakeasy. When you ask about the last topic, he tells you to commit the word “Charleston” into memory. Leave the building and take a taxi to the 12th Street Docks.

These are the same docks that we saw in the introduction to the game, and the same ship can be seen here a well. You see people in the distance getting off the ship. As soon as Laura gets out of her taxi, Steve Dorian, the stevedore, will appear. Talk to him and ask him about Pippin Carter, Archibald Carrington (to add Countess W-C to the list of topics), and the Leyendecker Museum. Asking about the museum will cause Steve to tell you that Carrington's Egyptian crates will be delivered there. Get a taxi to the speakeasy.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

As always, you can ask Steve about other topics in your notebook, although he doesn't say much. However, make sure you ask about the Leyendecker last. If you don't, Steve will terminate the conversation and get back to work.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt; 

Welcome to the speakeasy, the building disguised as a flower shop. Knock on the door (to the left of the “Drink Moxie” sign). When the bouncer says the Speakeasy is closed, select “Wait! I know the secret word”. from the dialog box that appears, then select “Charleston” from your notebook (in the Misc. section) to be allowed entry. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

It's not safe for girls to be out at night. If you stay in this location for too long, someone will come by and attack Laura with a knife.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

The speakeasy is filled with dancers having a good time. The only people Laura can interact with are the people at the table on the right, but the only person we need to talk to is the man in the black tuxedo suit, Ziggy. Talk to him. When he asks who sent you, select Rhubarb from your notebook. You can now talk to him about all topics in your notebook, then ask about the person called Ramses Najeer.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

If you ask about Egyptology, Ziggy will say that he was approached by Najeer and given two riddles. Both of them will come important later.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave the speakeasy and call a taxi. You will get a different driver this time, a dirty bastard who hasn't bothered to clean the back seat. When you get a chance to respond after he is rude to Laura, select either option. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

If you select the second option, the taxi driver will kick you out and you have to call a taxi again.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Now, sort through the trash until you find a yellow object, then examine it in inventory to find that it is a claim ticket from Lo Fat's Laundry. Get the driver to take you to Lo Fat's. Enter and give the claim ticket to Lo Fat, who gives you the evening gown Laura needs to wear at the museum. Take a taxi back to the Speakeasy and get inside the same way you did before. Upon entering, you are greeted by a slapper lying on the couch. Make Laura change in her evening gown and leave.   

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

There is nothing you can do with the slapper on the couch, so don't even try.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave the speakeasy and the game automatically takes you to the Museum, and this concludes this first act.



Act 2: Suspects on Parade
The Dagger of Amon Ra 

Walkthrough by *Katakis* (&lt;a class=&quot;__cf_email__&quot; href=&quot;/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection&quot; data-cfemail=&quot;f99b95928e96959fc9c8b99e94989095d79a9694&quot;&gt;[email protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;script cf-hash='f9e31' type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
/* &lt;![CDATA[ */!function(){try{var t=&quot;currentScript&quot;in document?document.currentScript:function(){for(var t=document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;script&quot;),e=t.length;e--;)if(t[e].getAttribute(&quot;cf-hash&quot;))return t[e]}();if(t&amp;&amp;t.previousSibling){var e,r,n,i,c=t.previousSibling,a=c.getAttribute(&quot;data-cfemail&quot;);if(a){for(e=&quot;&quot;,r=parseInt(a.substr(0,2),16),n=2;a.length-n;n+=2)i=parseInt(a.substr(n,2),16)^r,e+=String.fromCharCode(i);e=document.createTextNode(e),c.parentNode.replaceChild(e,c)}}}catch(u){}}();/* ]]&gt; */&lt;/script&gt;)

&lt;hr&gt;
* ACT 2 – Suspects on Parade
&lt;hr&gt;

After the taxi drops you off, go up the steps and greet Wolf Heimlich, the chief of security, who tells you that you need an invitation for the event. You don't have an invitation, but you can give him the press pass. The time will reach 7:00, so enter. Laura will arrive in the rotunda, which is filled with people getting comfortable.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Most of this act involves getting to know the other guests. As well as asking them about everything in your notebook, you must eavesdrop on 14 conversations between different groups, which will take place in different areas of the rotunda. The conversations have important information that you should take note of later. The groups are listed below:

Center Area: Ziggy, Dr. Pippin Carter, Yvette Delacroix, Ramses Najeer, and Dr. Carrington  

Center Area: Ziggy, Dr. Carter, Ramses, and Dr. Carrington 
 
Left Area: Yvette and Detective Ryan O'Riley 
 
Left Area: O'Riley and Dr. “Tut” Smith 

Center Area: Ramses and Countess Waldorf-Carlton 
 
Center Area: Ziggy and the Countess 
 
Right Area: Ziggy and Yvette 

Right Area: Yvette and Dr. Carrington 

Right Area: O'Riley and Ziggy 

Center Area: Yvette, Ramses, and Dr. Smith 

Left Area: Yvette, Dr. Myklos, and the Countess 
 
Left Area: Dr. Carter and Yvette 

Left Area: Dr. Carter and Dr. Smith 

Center Area: Steve and Yvette 
 

To eavesdrop, have Laura walk behind the group having the conversation.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

This is your final opportunity to talk to Steve Dorian. After this act, you won't be able to talk to him again.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Go to the left and get a glass from the table. Go into the gift shoppe to the right and look around. Look at the display case full of daggers and use the magnifying glass on each dagger until Laura finds one that hasn't got the words “Made in Pittsburg” etched on the blade. The time advances to 7:30, causing Heimlich to appear and telling Laura that the gift shop is closed. It shouldn't have been opened in the first place.

After Laura has been escorted outside, walk to the center area again to meet up with Dorian, who tells Laura that he only came here just to see her. The two have a serious conversation outside, Laura accepts Steve's invitation to dinner, and they share a little kiss (even though Laura has only met him for twenty minutes). 

Inside, you can proceed through the doorway in the center area to reach the Mastodon exhibit, which was off-limits before. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

1. From here on out, the different rooms that you enter contain exhibits that work just like real ones. A lot of research has been put into the game, and clicking the eye cursor on different objects, or using the magnifying glass on them, will give you a detailed background on each object. 

2. Walk around the museum for a minute and explore each room. It is important to memorize where each room is, as they will become important later.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Go east to the pterodactyl exhibit and walk through the north doorway to the Tyrannosaurus Rex. Look at the dinosaur bone on display to the left and pick it up (no joke). Head for the Egyptian exhibit and walk left to see three sarcophagi against the wall and a piece of Rosetta Stone on the left wall. Look at both of these, and examine them with your magnifying glass.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Important:

You must hover it over each hieroglyph so that all the hieroglyphs are recorded in Laura's notebook. You have plenty of time to do this; but if you don't do this by Act Five, you will lose the game.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
  
Below the third sarcophagus is a gold ankh medallion lying in a pool of blood. Look at it, then examine it with the magnifying glass to notice the initials P.S. etched into it. Look at the footprint, then examine it with the magnifying glass. 

Finally, open the third sarcophagus. Dr. Pippin Carter has been murdered, stabbed through the heart, blood gushing out of his wound. The murder weapon looks like a replica of the Dagger of Amon Ra. Look at, and examine with the magnifying glass, Carter's face, his clothing, the dagger, and the blood. Now, search his tuxedo to discover a notepad, and look at it to discover some unreadable writing on it. Take the notepad and leave the close-up view. The time will advance to 8:15 and O'Riley will come in to investigate the source of Laura's scream. She is instructed not to leave the building, and the act ends.


Act 3: On the Cutting Edge
The Dagger of Amon Ra 

Walkthrough by *Katakis* (&lt;a class=&quot;__cf_email__&quot; href=&quot;/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection&quot; data-cfemail=&quot;f1939d9a869e9d97c1c0b1969c90989ddf929e9c&quot;&gt;[email protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;script cf-hash='f9e31' type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
/* &lt;![CDATA[ */!function(){try{var t=&quot;currentScript&quot;in document?document.currentScript:function(){for(var t=document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;script&quot;),e=t.length;e--;)if(t[e].getAttribute(&quot;cf-hash&quot;))return t[e]}();if(t&amp;&amp;t.previousSibling){var e,r,n,i,c=t.previousSibling,a=c.getAttribute(&quot;data-cfemail&quot;);if(a){for(e=&quot;&quot;,r=parseInt(a.substr(0,2),16),n=2;a.length-n;n+=2)i=parseInt(a.substr(n,2),16)^r,e+=String.fromCharCode(i);e=document.createTextNode(e),c.parentNode.replaceChild(e,c)}}}catch(u){}}();/* ]]&gt; */&lt;/script&gt;)

&lt;hr&gt;
* ACT 3 – On the Cutting Edge
&lt;hr&gt;

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Throughout this act, you may see other staff members walking around the museum. If so, then this is your opportunity to ask them about topics in your notebook. They may have got some interesting things to say. Any new topics that show up in the notebook later, you can ask them about as well.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Act Three begins with Laura watching O'Riley question Dr. Carrington, the Countess, and Yvette about Dr. Carter's murder. We are also introduced to Ernie Leach who asks Laura to come by his office later. Go to the Master's Gallery. 

Look at the paintings until you find Hieronymus Bosch's “A Heartwarming Story”. Get a close-up view of the painting with your magnifying glass. There is a gold glint in the container. Examine it to find a silver key. Try to take the key to find out that it is embedded into the painting and can't be removed. Examine it to find some markings on it. Leave the close-up and go south to the room with the Thinking Man. 

The door to the the right leads to Yvette's office, and you hear some muffled voices behind it. Let's use the glass on the door to eavesdrop on a conversation between Yvette and Dr. Myklos. After joking with Dr. Myklos, Yvette whispers to her ear about a problem she is having as she doesn't want anyone to hear. It's as if she knows that Laura is eavesdropping on her. Go south to end up in Dr. Myklos's office. 

Here, look around and then remove the white cloth covering something on the floor. It's the other half of the Rosetta Stone. Look at it, then examine it to reveal some hieroglyphs on it, these ones are marked N-Z. Now Laura has the full set of hieroglyphs. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Remember:

It is important to hover your magnifying glass over each hieroglyph so that Laura records them in her notebook.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Try to take the snake oil on the desk but Dr. Myklos will come in and take it. She will explain that it is used to repel snakes, such as the cobras she found in the basement. She will mention Barney, her pet snake in the cage to the left of her desk. Look at the chalkboard, and examine it with the magnifying glass. It is a coded message, a poem which you should take the time to decode as some words will become important later.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

If you click on the animal skull on Dr. Myklos's desk, a hidden passage to the Preservation Lab will open up. Make sure Laura has the lantern with her before going into the passage. This action does not work later in the game.

Also, like many other secret passages waiting to be discovered, this passage is a one-way street.  Laura cannot go back the way she came.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave to notice Dr. Myklos going off to the right and the statue's head bent up. Go into Yvette's office. Here, look around. Search the trashcan and get the carbon paper inside. In inventory, examine it with the magnifying glass to find out that it has some words that cannot be read. Click the eye cursor on the desk lamp to bring a close-up view of it. Since the lamp is already on, use the paper on it to reveal a message for Ernie regarding a fencing job. It seems that he handles stolen goods from the museum to help pay off some gambling debts he has. Turn the lamp off and leave. We actually need that light bulb, but it's still hot to handle. While we are waiting for it to cool down, open the door on the right and enter Dr. Carrington's office.

As soon as we entered, muffled voices can be heard from the other side of the door, and we should eavesdrop on a conversation between Yvette and Ramses. She shows him her “love line” on the palm of her hand, and mentions a secret door somewhere in the museum where ceremonies are held.  When the conversion ends, look at the notepad on Carrington's desk and read the writing. He needs to see the Countess and Ziggy at 1:00 a.m. in the medieval armor display. Look at the purple thing at the left of the notepad to look at the phone list up close. Open it and examine the list. Now, note down the Be Safe's number and remove the picture above the fireplace to reveal a safe. 

The safe's combination is the number you wrote down earlier. Enter this in and the safe opens, revealing a personal diary belonging to Sterling Waldorf-Carlton, the previous museum's curator. Examine it with the magnifying glass to find about his fears, that the Countess only married him for his money, and that she is planning to kill him. Yvette fears her as well. Look at the intercom on the desk and press the left button above the six buttons together to turn the intercom on, then press the button underneath that. This will allow Laura to eavesdrop on a conversation between Heimlich and Dr. Myklos.

Heimlich has tattoos that Dr. Myklos admires, and he is more than happy to show them to her. He also gives her a bone which he has been carrying around for years. Press the next button on the intercom to listen in on Yvette and O'Riley. Yvette is impressed with the way O'Riley gets fit by doing sit-ups fifty times a day. It looks like Yvette is about to get close to O'Riley. Press the third button. Ziggy is in some place he shouldn't be, and Leach orders him to leave before he hurts him. That's all the conversations Laura can listen to for now.

Return to Yvette's office and bring a close-up view of the desk lamp again. Examine the light bulb and take it. Leave the office and touch the statue's head. Go to the right to find that the head affects whether the entrance to the basement opens up. There are steps leading down, but the light bulb has blown. Replace it with the light bulb you just picked up. Climb down the steps to reach another doorway, and another one to the right. To the left is a glass alcove. Look at it, then break the glass with the dinosaur bone and take the lantern. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Sometimes when you smash the glass, Heimlich will appear and kick Laura out. If this happens, just come back and keep smashing the glass until you can get the lantern.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Open the north doorway to enter Heimlich's office. Wait a few seconds, and the intercom crackles to life. It's Dr. Myklos, who tells Heimlich to meet her in the armor display at 2:00 so that he can show her his private scars. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

There are plenty of ways you can die in Heimlich's office. For example, don't mess with the weapons or the mousetrap.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Use the dinosaur bone on the mousetrap and a machine gun will appear and blast it to bits. You can now get the cheese that was in it. Now, look at the bookcase and search the shelves until you find a book stuffed in there backwards. Remove it from the bookshelf. It is a book of poems. Open it up and get the garter. In inventory, look at it to discover that it belongs to Yvette, who left a note attached to it. Examine the garter with the magnifying glass to read it. She tells Wolfie that he can have the other half if she meets her at 3 a.m. in the Preservation Lab. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Click on the bottom-most picture to the right of the bookcase to reveal a button, then click the button up a secret passage to Dr. Carrington's office. Once again, it is important to have the lantern with you.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave Wolfie's office and go through the doorway on the right. This is the Preservation Lab. You will hear voices coming from the other side of that doorway to the east. You know what to do. Ernie notices the tattoo of the Eiffel Tower that Yvette has been carrying, and that he has some gambling debts.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Even though it isn't compulsory to winning the game, you can have Laura walk into the same office Yvette was talking to another staff member and see her making out with them. The only exception to this is the conversation between Yvette and Dr. Smith, which occurs much later in the game.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

See what's on the other side of the doorway to the far north. It looks like a store room. Dr. Myklos is here, and she tells Laura that she is looking for her pet ferret Daisy who has hiding out in the room. Leave and go upstairs. Go west. Muffled voices are coming from the other side of Yvette's door, s listen in on the conversation. O'Riley tells Yvette how she loves him and threatens to kill her if he finds out that she is sleeping with someone. He thinks that there are criminals in the police force, who are happy enough to accept a bribe then regret it later.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

You may be thinking how Yvette managed to get inside her office to meet O'Riley when she was just in Ernie's, and how could Laura not see her do this. 
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Go to the Egyptian exhibit and wait there until 10:15. Dr. Smith will appear. Laura questions him what he is doing here and about Dr. Carter's murder, which he doesn't know about yet. Just before he leaves, ask him about the ankh medallion. Walk left and open the sarcophagus you found Dr. Carter's body in. Where is he? Leave and go to the armor display. Look at the helmet of the knight facing the screen and examine it with the magnifying glass, then take it off. So someone has stuffed Carter's body in the armor. Look at and examine him with the magnifying glass. Go east where murder number two occurred.

Whoever was killed here had his head severed and impaled by the pterodactyl. Look at the body, the blood, and both hands. Look at the pterodactyl, and examine everything with your magnifying glass. Search the pockets and you will find nothing. Two questions: who cut off his head, and where is the head? Exit the close-up. The time will advance to 11:15. Go into the life mask room. Something strange is here, something that doesn't look right. There, next to Japan. Examine it. It's Ziggy. So that's who the dead body belonged to. 

Look at dead Ziggy, then examine him with the magnifying glass. There's nothing else you can do with him, so leave the close-up view. Heimlich and O'Riley appear to investigate Laura's scream. Heimlich threatens to interrogate her, but O'Riley talks him out of it. After the two of them argue for a bit, they leave. Go down into the basement and use the glass on Heimlich's office door to hear Dr. Myklos talking to somebody. 

Walk into the Preservation Lab then walk back out again and do the same thing to find out that she is actually talking to Daisy. Repeat what you just did. This time, when you put the glass to the door, Dr. Myklos is telling Ramses that she noticed him admiring his swords in the armor display and offers to show him Heimlich's latest specimen. Ramses feels uncomfortable toward Dr. Myklos's fascination with his tattoo on one of his ankles. 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Unlike other doors where conversations took place, this one is locked. That means that Laura can't humiliate Ramses by walking into Heimlich's office.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Put the glass against Heimlich's office door to overhear yet another conversation. Heimlich and Dr. Myklos is in there discussing the Countess, who has been seen going in and out of the museum after hours. They also discuss killing her if she is seen again. So, are they joking about murdering her, or is their plan for real?   

Go upstairs to Yvette's office. Look at the paper cutter, then examine it with the magnifying glass. The liquid on the blade is either red ink or blood. Go into Dr. Carrington's office to discover him lying on the desk, thrown into his own stuffed porcupine statue. Notice how Laura gets startled rather than screaming. Look at him, the porcupine quills, and the blood on the desktop, then examine them with the magnifying glass. (If you examine the blood, you will notice the letters C.P. written on it.) Also look at the clock and the notepad. Leave the close-up and the time will advance to 12:45.

Search the bookshelf until you find a book called Crime and Punishment, by clicking the eye cursor on different areas. (That's what C.P. stood for.) Remove it from the bookshelf and look at it. Now, examine it with the magnifying glass to see something poking out from it. Open it to discover a police file inside. Examine it to see a handwritten note saying “Remember our deal”. Get the file and look at it in inventory to read a file concerning Watney Little, a con man who was investigated by Scotland Yard and wanted for a series of offenses. He recently escaped from Dartmoor Prison. Ziggy told us about a con man earlier. This must be him.

Go down to the Preservation Lab and go into Ernie's office. Look around here. Look at the stolen goods that adorn the north and east walls.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

Spend too much time here, and Ernie will come into his office and kick Laura out. You won't be able to get back in here after that.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Shortly on the intercom, Dr. Myklos will tell Ernie to investigate a jammed release valve on Tank number thirteen. Look on the floor beside Ernie's desk and get the snake lasso. Open Ernie's toolbox and get the pliers. Look at the Alcohol Vat Book on the desk and open it up. Look at the page which details the contents of each of the fourteen vats. According to the book, Tank #13 is supposed to contain warthogs. So why is the release valve jammed?

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Trivia:

Vat #14 contains the remains of King Edward of Daventry, a reference to &lt;a href=&quot;/search/quick?game=Quest+%2b+Crown&quot;&gt;King's Quest&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave the office and look at the tanks until you find Vat 13, and when you do, click the Hand cursor on it. Laura will climb up and use a pole to search through the liquid, and eventually finds the Dagger of Amon Ra. So why was that in the vat, and what was it doing there? Was somebody hiding it in there? 

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

Feel free to check out the other vats. But if you open too many tanks at random, the fumes from the alcohol will make Laura pass out and the game ends.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
 
Leave and head on over to the Masters Gallery. Since we have the pliers, we can use them to get the skeleton key from Bosch's painting. Once you have the key, go into Dr. Carrington's office and listen in on the conversation about to take place. Yvette is asking Dr. Smith to move her desk to hide a red stain on the rug. When the conversation ends, look in the fireplace and get the piece of charcoal. In inventory, use the charcoal on Dr. Carter's notepad. Looking at it reveals three of his appointments. Carter was supposed to meet Yvette at 8:00, but at that time he was murdered instead. Go to the armor display and hide behind the large tapestry on the left to advance time to 1:00.

The Countess walks in carrying a painting, expecting Ziggy and Dr. Carrington to show up. Once she stops moving, confront her. Laura grills her, and the Countess is offended that she is branded a thief. However, she later confesses that she is an art burglar, who gets someone to duplicate the real paintings and hang them up in the Masters Gallery. The real paintings are then sold to private collectors. That's why Bosch's painting was wet. Start asking her questions by clicking the question mark talk cursor on her.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

You only have a second or two to do this before the Countess makes her way off the screen.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Ask her about Sterling W-C's diary to have Laura grill her about it. The Countess is threatening toward Laura, but doesn't seem to care that O' Riley may find out about here. Go into the pterodactyl exhibit. Here, look at Ziggy's body and use the wire cutters to take the wires with you. Now, return to the Preservation Lab and proceed north into the storeroom.

Wait for a few seconds and Daisy will appear and sniff out the steamer trunk underneath the workbench. Open the freezer to the left of the storage crates and get the slab of meat. Now, open the trunk will the skeleton key and throw the meat in there. The Egyptian beetles inside, happy with the meat, go out of the trunk and march off with it.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

You need to do this quickly. If you're too slow, the beetles will jump out and eat Laura's flesh. It's not a pretty sight.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Look inside the trunk. You remember in the introduction, a man was strangled and put inside the steamer trunk? Well, this is him right here, the bugs reducing him to a skeleton. He has something dangling around his neck. Examine it with the magnifying glass, and click the hand cursor on it to open it up. There is an inscription on the back of the watch. Look at it. It says that the watch is awarded to Dr. Carrington for his years of service. Actually, the skeleton belongs to the real Dr. Carrington, who we saw get murdered on the Andrea Doria. So who went around impersonating Carrington this whole time, and why did he turn up dead in his office? Get the watch and the time advances to 1:45. Get the snake oil on top of the workbench (you'll need this later). and leave.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

Go back to Ernie's office and press the button the wall. Something moves in the distance. Leave the office and go into the storeroom and a secret passage appears that lead back up to the Egyptian exhibit. If Laura tries to enter the passage without the lantern, she will be attacked by bats. 
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Leave and proceed on to the Thinking Man room and use the glass to listen in on whatever conversation Yvette is having with something. She accuses O'Riley about lying about him playing a part of the burglary of the dagger, and that Ziggy told her all about it. But O'Riley says that he is lying about it. Go to the armor display and hide behind the tapestry just in time for the meeting with Dr. Myklos and Heimlich.

Olympia talks to him about his scars and her interest in taking over the museum someday. They also know that Laura is hiding behind the tapestry. Go to the mastodon exhibit and there you will see Ernie slouching over its tusks. Look at him, then examine him with the magnifying glass. When you examine the body, you discover animal hairs that were draped in alcohol. Ernie must have been placed in one of the tanks in the Preservation Lab, along with whatever animal there was in there, and thrown over the mastodon's tusks. But what was Ernie doing looking inside the tanks? Get the hairs and exit the close-up.

After the time advances to 2:15, go into the Master's Gallery where you see Heimlich interrogating O'Riley. Laura tells them that Ernie has been murdered. As usual, Heimlich is an asshole about it, but O'Riley says that he will investigate. This is the end of Act Three.  



Act 4: The Museum of the Dead
The Dagger of Amon Ra 

Walkthrough by *Katakis* (&lt;a class=&quot;__cf_email__&quot; href=&quot;/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection&quot; data-cfemail=&quot;f597999e829a9993c5c4b59298949c99db969a98&quot;&gt;[email protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;script cf-hash='f9e31' type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
/* &lt;![CDATA[ */!function(){try{var t=&quot;currentScript&quot;in document?document.currentScript:function(){for(var t=document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;script&quot;),e=t.length;e--;)if(t[e].getAttribute(&quot;cf-hash&quot;))return t[e]}();if(t&amp;&amp;t.previousSibling){var e,r,n,i,c=t.previousSibling,a=c.getAttribute(&quot;data-cfemail&quot;);if(a){for(e=&quot;&quot;,r=parseInt(a.substr(0,2),16),n=2;a.length-n;n+=2)i=parseInt(a.substr(n,2),16)^r,e+=String.fromCharCode(i);e=document.createTextNode(e),c.parentNode.replaceChild(e,c)}}}catch(u){}}();/* ]]&gt; */&lt;/script&gt;)

&lt;hr&gt;
* ACT 4 – Museum of the Dead
&lt;hr&gt;

Go to Yvette's office to see Yvette sitting in a chair. She is depressed that Ernie has been killed, possibly by this “Icepick” fellow. When Laura leaves her office, she encounters Steve and Dr. Myklos, and Dr. Myklos has just admired some of Steve's scars. Maybe she is cheating on Heimlich? Laura and Steve have a conversation, and we find that Steve is obviously distracted. Their conversation is cut off when Yvette walks out of her office and tells her that Ernie is dead and what would she ever do without him. She invites Steve to her office to talk about the matter, and he accepts her invitation.

That gives us all the more reason to eavesdrop on her conversation. It isn't a conversation at all. It sounds like Steve is giving Yvette a massage, and she is getting turned on. Laura investigates and finds him just giving her a shoulder rub. When she leaves, go to the Preservation Lab to make the clock advance to 3 a.m. There is supposed to be a meeting between Heimlich, Watney Little, and Yvette in this very room, but no one has turned up.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Note:

By the way, if you see the Countess walking around, ask her about the pocket watch for an interesting reaction from her.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Look at the container of snake oil on the workbench to the left. This is where you can fill up your bottle of snake oil for an event that occurs later in the game. Now let's see if Steve is still with Yvette in her office. We go inside Yvette's office, only to find out there were signs of a struggle. Look at the desk. Look at the shoe, the red hairs, a part of Yvette's dress, and examine everything with the magnifying glass. Proceed to the Master's Gallery.

There is a new piece of art here. Who did this? If you remember, Steve told us that he was into sculpturing. Look at it, then click the hand cursor on it. Break Steve's creation by using the dinosaur bone on it. The sculpture will crumble, revealing Yvette. Look at her. It's not a pretty sight. Look at her face and the stocking around her neck. So Steve strangled Yvette with her own stocking and made her into a piece of art. Look at and examine the two pieces of evidence – the bifocal glasses and two red hairs – then take them both. Who knew that Steve is a murderer? Leave the close-up view.

Head to the armor display. Near the small pool of blood on the floor is a boot. Look at it and examine it with the magnifying glass to get its size. Get the boot. Look at the blood and also examine it also. This must be Steve's blood. Did Yvette lash out at him in this room for some reason and paid the price? Go to the Thinking Man room to trigger a meanwhile sequence. Dr. Myklos finds the Countess in her office, strangled on top of her desk. She utters O'Riley's name. It is possible that Heimlich did this to her as he and Dr. Myklos planned her death earlier, and she is asking O'Riley for help. Or, perhaps she is accusing O'Riley. Either way, we can't be sure yet.

When Dr. Myklos comes out of her office, she tells Laura about her and that she suspects that she has been bitten by a snake. When she leaves, go into her office. A cobra will appear and start hissing at Laura. Who released it from its cage? Use the snake oil on the cobra (x3) to lure it into the corner to the right of Dr. Myklos's desk, then use the snake lasso on it. Finally, put the cobra back where it belongs.

Now that the cobra has been taken care of, you can go ahead and look at the Countess. Look at the Countess (her face, body, and legs) then examine her right leg with the magnifying glass to notice the bite on her ankle. Now, examine her body with the magnifying glass and get the smelling salts. Look at and examine the bite. Look at and examine the bunch of grapes to the right of the body. Get the grapes then leave the close-up view and the office.



Act 5: Rex Takes a Bite Out of Crime
The Dagger of Amon Ra 

Walkthrough by *Katakis* (&lt;a class=&quot;__cf_email__&quot; href=&quot;/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection&quot; data-cfemail=&quot;6d0f01061a02010b5d5c2d0a000c0401430e0200&quot;&gt;[email protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;script cf-hash='f9e31' type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
/* &lt;![CDATA[ */!function(){try{var t=&quot;currentScript&quot;in document?document.currentScript:function(){for(var t=document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;script&quot;),e=t.length;e--;)if(t[e].getAttribute(&quot;cf-hash&quot;))return t[e]}();if(t&amp;&amp;t.previousSibling){var e,r,n,i,c=t.previousSibling,a=c.getAttribute(&quot;data-cfemail&quot;);if(a){for(e=&quot;&quot;,r=parseInt(a.substr(0,2),16),n=2;a.length-n;n+=2)i=parseInt(a.substr(n,2),16)^r,e+=String.fromCharCode(i);e=document.createTextNode(e),c.parentNode.replaceChild(e,c)}}}catch(u){}}();/* ]]&gt; */&lt;/script&gt;)

&lt;hr&gt;
* ACT 5 – Rex Takes a Bite out of Crime
&lt;hr&gt;

From here on out, it is going to get dangerous. Laura is being chased by the killer in a black robe through the museum, with a mace in his hand. But we don't know who the killer is. Could it be Heimlich, who had it in for Laura ever seen she discovered the first murder before anyone else? As for what the title of this act means, it is a hint on how to deal with the killer.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Important:

In addition to recording the hieroglyphs on both halves of the Rosetta stone, make sure you have the following inventory items before proceeding: wire, wire cutters, snake lasso, snake oil, lantern, cheese. If any of these items are missing, restore an earlier save game. The game cannot be completed if you don't have any of these.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

The chase begins in the mastodon room, and the killer appears from the right. Go right into the pterodactyl exhibit and close the doors, then wire them shut. Go into the armor display, close the door, and pull down the bar over it (click the hand cursor on it). Now, go north and move the chair in front of the locked door. Stand on top of it and open the window on top. That's going to distract him. Proceed into the Egyptian exhibit.

Go left and hide in the first sarcophagus. The killer appears briefly. Failing to find Laura, he leaves and breaks down a door. Get out of the sarcophagus. Leave the exhibit and go through the broken doorway into the cargo area. Push the crate suspended in the air so that it blocks the open doorway. Use the wire cutters on the cable to lower the crate. Push the crate on the right to reveal a doorway then open it to enter an elevator. Pull the lever to go down to a room containing sarcophagi.

The killer has called the elevator. It won't take long for him to get here. Close the door behind you and take the mummy from the open sarcophagus on the floor. Use the mummy on the door to prop the mummy up against it. Look at the mummy on the left closest to the door. Look at the snake symbol on its headdress. Use the snake lasso on it. Something clicks inside. Open the sarcophagus and enter the secret passage.

Laura interrupts a secret ceremony in the basement and is caught intruding. Ramses Najeer and someone else grabs her. Ramses is into ceremonies, and if you have clicked the eye cursor on him in Act Two, you would have known that already. He says that Laura must be detained, for fear that she might spill the secrets relating to the ceremonies. Ramses is ready to sacrifice Laura unless she is willing to pass a test. The test only consists of the same two questions Ziggy told us in Act One, and the answers are hidden on Dr. Myklos's chalkboard in her office. After Laura tells Ramses about the killer, he tells her to leave through the secret escape route, which leads her to the furnace room.

Below the chute on the right is the coal bin with a boot hanging out of it. Look at the coal bin. Steve is under the coal. Click the hand cursor just to the left of the shovel to uncover Steve's face, then use the smelling salts on him. As he starts to get up, give him his other boot.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Warning:

If you don't give him the boot, Steve will get up anyway. He will then step on something and fall unconscious. Also, wait too long to do anything and Laura will be shot by the killer. 
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

With Steve's help, click on the hand cursor on the mural to uncover a hole, then click the hand cursor on it so that the two of you enter. As soon as you do, turn on the lantern. There are cobras on the other side of the passageway. Use the snake oil on them. The cobra do not like it, turn around, then leave the passageway, allowing you to continue. When Laura and Steve make their way to the second area of the passageway, the exit is blocked by rats and gunfire is heard from the direction of the furnace room. Throw the cheese over either one of the openings. Click the walk cursor on the right doorway. 

Laura and Steve will come out through Rex's mouth. Quickly press the button on the right. The killer will try to leave the same way, but will be trapped between Rex's jaws.



Act 6: The Coroner's Inquest
The Dagger of Amon Ra 

Walkthrough by *Katakis* (&lt;a class=&quot;__cf_email__&quot; href=&quot;/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection&quot; data-cfemail=&quot;fe9c929589919298cecfbe99939f9792d09d9193&quot;&gt;[email protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;script cf-hash='f9e31' type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;
/* &lt;![CDATA[ */!function(){try{var t=&quot;currentScript&quot;in document?document.currentScript:function(){for(var t=document.getElementsByTagName(&quot;script&quot;),e=t.length;e--;)if(t[e].getAttribute(&quot;cf-hash&quot;))return t[e]}();if(t&amp;&amp;t.previousSibling){var e,r,n,i,c=t.previousSibling,a=c.getAttribute(&quot;data-cfemail&quot;);if(a){for(e=&quot;&quot;,r=parseInt(a.substr(0,2),16),n=2;a.length-n;n+=2)i=parseInt(a.substr(n,2),16)^r,e+=String.fromCharCode(i);e=document.createTextNode(e),c.parentNode.replaceChild(e,c)}}}catch(u){}}();/* ]]&gt; */&lt;/script&gt;)

&lt;hr&gt;
* ACT 6 – The Coroner's Inquest
&lt;hr&gt;

In this sixth and final act, Laura is attending an inquest. In attendance are the Coroner and his assistant; your boss, Sam Augustini; and two photographers. Laura has to answer a lot of questions relating to both the murders and the theft of the Dagger of Amon Ra. In addition to this, the Coroner will automatically study all evidence Laura has in her inventory to see if she has the evidence to back up her responses to his questions. If you followed this walkthrough from start to finish, you won't have a problem with this. The answer to the questions are given below. 

Question: Who murdered Dr. Pippin Carter? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 

Motive: Financial Gain (or) Cover another crime 


Question: Who murdered Lawrence 'Ziggy' Ziegfeld? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 

Motive: Cover another crime 


Question: Who murdered Ernie Leach? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 

Motive: Cover another crime 


Question: Who murdered Yvette Delacroix? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 

Motive: Jealousy 


Question: Who murdered Countess Livinia Waldorf-Carlton? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 

Motive: Cover another crime 


Question: Who was the skeleton found in the steamer trunk? 

Answer: Dr. Archibald Carrington III 


Question: Who murdered Dr. Archibald Carrington? 

Answer: Watney Little 


Question: Who impersonated Dr. Archibald Carrington? 

Answer: Watney Little 


Question: Who murdered Watney Little? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 

Motive: Financial gain 


Question: Who actually stole the Dagger of Amon Ra from the ancient Egypt exhibit? 

Answer: Watney Little 


Question: Who manipulated Watney Little into stealing the Dagger of Amon Ra ? 

Answer: Detective Ryan Hanrahan O'Riley 


Question: Who was the woman involved in stealing paintings from the old Master's Gallery? 

Answer: Countess Waldorf-Carlton 


Question: Who was the man involved in stealing paintings from the old Master's Gallery? 

Answer: Watney Little 


Question: Who was the middleman who provided forged paintings for the Countess, and sold the real ones for her? 
 
Answer: Lawrence 'Ziggy' Ziegfeld 


Question: Who was the high priest for the Amon Ra sun worshippers? 
 
Answer: Ramses Najeer 


Question: Which museum employee runs a fencing operation as a sideline business?
 
Answer: Ernie Leach 


After these questions, Laura brings her eyewitness in, who happens to be Dr. Smith, who explains that O'Riley murdered two of his fellow worshippers in front of him before chasing Laura in Act Five. For her assistance to the investigation, Laura is awarded the Commendation of Valor from the New York Police Department. Her father, John, would be so proud of her!

Meanwhile, O'Riley is hammering coal at Dartmoor Prison, watched over by a few guards. He curses at Laura after each hit and vows to get revenge on her. Back at the 12th Street Docks, Steve gives Laura a copy of the dagger from the museum gift shop, and she accepts his invitation to dinner. Finally, the game gives an outline on what happened to each character.

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
Alternate Ending:

If you fail to answer the above questions properly, the Coroner will tell Laura what he thinks happened, and you will get the bad ending. There will be a different newspaper article saying that Laura bungled the investigation and you will witness her murder, blood and all.

You will also get this ending if you fail to examine the dead bodies and collected the evidence, even if you get the questions correct.
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;

Congratulations! You have just completed &lt;i&gt;The Dagger of Amon Ra&lt;/i&gt;.
</secrets>
  <genre>
   <line>
    <col>Adventure</col>
   </line>
  </genre>
 </item>
