 >
  <description>After travelling back and forth through time in the previous game, Roger Wilco is back in the Starfleet Acadamy, serving as both a cadet and a janitor. Cheating his way through the Starfleet Aptitude Test, Roger is finally given the rank of captain, his own ship (a garbage scow) and a mission: to explore strange new worlds (which no man in his right mind would explore), to seek out new life and new civilizations (which grew out of the massive amounts of trash Roger will collect on his way), to boldly go where no man has gone before. Step by step Roger will have to unveil a galaxy-wide biohazardous material dumping scheme, solve the mystery of the disappearance of a fellow Starfleet captain and his ship, and confront an agent of an old nemesis.

Space Quest V: The Next Mutation is an adventure game in the Space Quest series. Like its brethren, it is characterized by humorous writing and situations, as well as plenty of opportunities for the hero to die horribly. The game is entirely mouse-controlled: the player interacts with the world by clicking on locations, people and objects on the screen, cycling between various actions (walking, looking, touching or taking, talking, etc.), by clicking the right mouse button or using the icon bar. The latter also contains icons that allow the player to access Roger's inventory, quit the game or change the settings.

Commands for smelling and tasting have been removed, but a special icon for giving orders has been added. It can be used on any object or character in the game, but its actual purpose is to issue specific commands to the crew members: Roger's garbage scow, the Eureka, has a crew over which he presides. The game is plot-driven and contains cutscenes done in a comic book-like style. Plot development is linear, but each planet the protagonist visits usually consists of several screens and contains its own objectives and puzzles. There are also hazardous situations that may occur on the spaceship itself and must be dealt with.</description>
  <comments></comments>
  <secrets>How to catch Cliffy

There's a sequence in the middle of the game where you have to go in an emergency pod and catch your buddy Cliffy lost in space. On faster machines, it's absolutely impossible to do it: it's too fast, even if you reduce the game's speed to a minimum. However, if you download a slow-down utility like &quot;Turbo&quot; and set the speed of your computer to the lowest possible, the problem will be solved :)



Walkthrough
In &lt;i&gt;Space Quest V&lt;/i&gt;, Roger Wilco has just joined StarCon Academy as he tries his luck in the Bridge Simulator. He makes good progress when Captain Quirk interrupts him and orders Roger to go to class. He complies and goes to the corridor.

In the corridor, enter the classroom. The teacher tells Roger that the SAT is already in progress, and gives him his test. There are ten questions on the test, but you must get five correct. Since Roger is too lazy studying, cheating in necessary. But to combat cheating, StarCon has installed an anti-cheat droid in every classroom to be on the watch for cheaters. If someone is called cheating, they would be evicted from StarCon Academy. However, the droid doesn't do his job properly, and every five seconds, it will turn away from the students before continuing to watch them shortly after. When he does this, click on the black box on the desk of the student to your left to look at his test, and make sure which square is filled. Now look at your own test and fill in that box. Repeat this until the test is over.

You are told to clean the academy crest as punishment for being late to class. When you leave, go south and open the janitor' closet, then take the things that fall out. Go south again and go through the corridor that leads to the east. Go down the elevator platform to arrive at the crest. The crest is dirty, so it's time to clean it. But before you do, make sure that you put the cones down. If you don't, people will walk over the crest, putting more dirt on it. In inventory, click the floor-scrubber and then place it on the crest. Click the Hand cursor on it twice, once to open it up, then once more to use it. Click the Brush icon on the dirty areas to direct Roger there. Eventually, you will complete your task and the crest will sparkle. Captain Quirk and Beatrice will speak to Roger for a moment, then leave.

Go west to return Roger to the balcony. Go west to arrive back to the corridor. Watch the cut-scene that follows. Roger will be standing outside the StarCon conference room where he is told that the SAT results are posted on the bulletin board outside the classroom. Go south and you will find out that you have scored 100%, and that you are recommended to receive your command. 

You are placed on the &lt;i&gt;SCS Eureka&lt;/i&gt; as captain, and its crew introduce themselves. Droole is the navigation and weapons officer, and he is on the right. Flo is your communications operator, and she is on your left. After you have been introduced, sit in the captain's chair to be looking at the front view of the ship.  Click the Command cursor on Flo, and tell her to Hail StarCon. StarCon will clear the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; to take off. StarCon will tell Roger to take his ship to Gangularis, Peeyu, and Kiz Urazgubi for garbage pick-ups. Now tell Droole to Lay in a Course. You are asked which planet you want to go to. In &lt;i&gt;Galactic Inquirer&lt;/i&gt; magazine that came with the game, there will be a list of planets that you need to go to, and a five-digit number next to them. Enter the one for Gangularis.

Tell Droole to proceed at Regular Speed. As soon as the ship leaves StarCon, Droole will automatically go into Lite Speed. When the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; disappears, a ship materializes. The android in the ship, known as WD40, finds out that Roger is wanted for mail fraud in &lt;moby game=&quot;sq2&quot;&gt;Space Quest II&lt;/a&gt;. Back inside the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;, tell Droole to proceed at Regular Speed after he tells you that they are nearing their destination. Tell Droole to Activate RRS after Flo tells Roger that she is tracking a waste beacon. If all goes well, the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; should suck up the floating bag of trash. Shortly, you are told that a life-form is in the waste compartment. Leave the front view by clicking Exit and get him out of the chair, then walk through the door to the north to enter the engineering section. There is a waste compartment here. Press the black button beside it to open the compartment. Whatever was in the garbage bag will fall out and land Roger in it. When he gets up to look inside, he gets out a six-legged alien creature. Prying the creature off, he names the creature Spike. Spike is released from Roger's grip, and then takes off.

Open the toolbox on the left and get the fuse, the hole punch, the cutting torch, and the antacid tablets. Close the toolbox and open the door to the science lab. Inside, walk Roger around the lab and Spike will appear and jump onto Roger's face. (If he does not, leave the room and re-enter.) While Roger hangs on to Spike, open the red specimen tank on the east wall and drop Spike in, as well as the tablets to keep his acid from ruining the place. Now walk back to the bridge and sit in the captain's chair. Command Droole to Lay in a Course for Peeyu, and enter the co-ordinates for that planet. Command Droole to go to Lite Speed, and wait until he tells Roger that they are nearing their destination. Command him to go to Regular Speed, and wait until Flo tells Roger that she is tracking a waste beacon. Command Droole to Activate RRS. The &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; will suck up another bag of trash. After this, the ship will intercept a transmission from StarCon. After the transmission is terminated, command Droole to Lay in a Course for Kiz Urazgubi.

You know, if you pronounce the name of the planet correctly, it sounds more like Kiss your ass good-bye, and it's obviously why it is called that. WD40 materializes her ship; and decloaks, attacks, and disables the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;. She gives Roger five standard time units to beam down to the planet's surface before she opens fire on the ship. Unless you want her to do so, return to the lab. Stand on the transporter and click on it with the Command icon to beam Roger down to the surface. 

Once he is on the surface, WD40 lands, cloaks her ship, then flies off to find him. Once Roger emerge from the cave located above the pond, go east to arrive at a chasm. Go north along the narrow tree. Roger will get across, then fall into the pond, taking a dead branch with him. Once you get out of the pool, get the branch and return to the chasm. Use the Walk cursor to crawl through the hollow log. Halfway, Roger will stop and you see his eyes appearing out of the hole. 

Click the Walk cursor again to climb out of the  log. Now use the branch on the clusters of green fruit hanging above you to make them swing, then quickly get a piece of fruit. Crawl Roger back through the log and go west. Walk Roger into the cave leading north to emerge at the top of the waterfall. Go to the cave leading north. WD40 appears and follows him. From where Roger emerges next, click the Walk cursor on the ledge across from him and Roger will leap across to it. 

Climb up to the boulder and wait until WD40 enters the cave. Use the branch on the boulder. When WD40 is knocked out of the cave into the pool below, climb back down to the ledge, jump back across, then make you way to the pool. Colored lights appear in the pool. As soon as WD40 flies out of the water, crawl Roger halfway through the log. WD40 will land on the log above Roger. At this point, shove the piece of fruit up the tailpipe of the jetpack. WD40 flies off then explode mid-air. Get out of the log and go west. Pick up WD40's head off the ground, then walk back to the spot where you beamed down. Cliffy, the ship's engineer, will be there to beam you back up to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;.

When on board, leave the science lab and re-enter. Cliffy appears with WD40's parts and gives Roger the device she used to cloak her ship. Walk over to the transporter and click the Command cursor on it. Roger will take Cliffy with him and both of you beam back down to the surface. You and Cliffy will automatically appear at WD40's ship. Click the device on Roger to open the ship and lower an elevator platform. Walk Roger onto it. Cliffy stays behind. When you get inside the ship, open the panel on the east wall to bring up a series of knobs, latches, and panels. Open the top latch to start the countdown. You have approximately five minutes before the ship blows up. Open the bottom latch. Turn the top-left knob and the bottom-right knob. Open the top-left panel and the bottom-right panel. Now turn the bottom-left knob followed by the top-right knob. Open the top-right panel and then the bottom-left panel. Take the cloaking device. Exit the ship via the elevator platform to automatically beam back up to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;.

Back in the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;, Roger gives the cloaking device to Cliffy, and Cliffy tell him that he's putting WD40 back together to serve as a member of the crew. Go to the bridge and sit down. Command Droole to Lay in a Course for the Spacebar. Command Droole to travel at Lite Speed. When he tells Roger that they are approaching their destination, command Droole to travel at Regular Speed, then command him to put the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; into Standard Orbit. When the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; orbits the Spacebar, the crew will beam down, expect you. Go into the science lab, remove Spike from the specimen tank, and beam him down to the Spacebar.

Inside the spacebar, head to your crew's table to sit down. Shortly, a merchant will come along and offer his wares to Roger. After refusing the offer, he is given a sample packet of dehydrated space monkeys. When the merchant leaves, Captain Quirk shows up to challenge Roger to a game called &lt;i&gt;Battle Cruiser&lt;/i&gt;. Similar to &lt;i&gt;Battleship&lt;/i&gt;, the objective is to sink all of Quirk's ships. You are presented with four starships and three ten-by-ten sectors to place them in. To fire, choose which of the opponent's sectors you wish to fire into, followed by the square on the grid where you want your shot to hit. You also are presented with two munitions. You have the regular photon torpedo, which can hit only one square on a sector grid. If you miss, a green marker appears showing where the shot has been hit. If you hit, a red marker appears. You also have a probe, which can reveal ships within a five-by-five area. If detected, the ships (or its parts) are revealed in a purple outline. The game is as simple as that. 

Note: Playing &lt;i&gt;Battle Cruiser&lt;/i&gt; is completely optional. The only disadvantage is that you won't get to score the maximum points.

After &lt;i&gt;Battle Cruiser&lt;/i&gt; is finished, Roger finds that Cliffy is fighting with a member of Quirk's crew, causing him to be thrown in the brig. Once Quirk leaves for his ship, the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;, sit down at your table and use the dehydrated space monkeys in your drink. The space monkeys will emerge from inside the drink, then they float around and multiply quickly, to the point where the Spacebar can lo longer handle the capacity. While this is happening, stand up and go east to arrive at the brig. Wait until the guards leave their post to investigate the alert that the space monkeys have caused, then use the Hand cursor on the control panel to turn off the invisible force field blocking the way to the cells. With that done, go north and inspect the second cell on the west wall. This is Cliffy's cell. Talk to Cliffy then place Spike on the bars. Spike will piddle acid on each of the bars, eating them away. Eventually, the three of you get beamed back to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;, and the crew make their escape before the Spacebar explodes.

The &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; is ordered to head for Klorox II for yet another garbage pick-up, so command Droole to Lay in a Course for Klorox II and then command him to travel at Lite Speed. When the ship arrives at Klorox II, command Droole to go to Regular Speed. Flo tells Roger that they aren't tracking a waste beacon. Command Droole to put the ship into Standard Orbit. When the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; is orbiting Klorox II, command Flo to Hail Ship. She will get the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;, and Quirk will tell Roger to get off the frequency as he tries to make his report. Once the conversation between the two has been terminated, leave the cockpit view and go to the science lan. Droole will join you. Place Spike back in the tank, stand on the transporter, and beam down to Klorox II with Droole.

Droole and Roger arrive south of the deserted remnants of the planet's one colony, and they agree to split up.  Go north into the colony's central building. Save the game, then use the computer console in the center of the room. A pukoid will attack him, and you have to dodge the death loogies that he drips down. Once you have dodge five loogies, Droole will appear and shoots the pukoid. The following cut-scene has the pukoid change back to a human, who tells Roger that there is a secret path to the west. He then dies. Get the piece of paper that the pukoid dropped earlier. Look at it and write down the number written on it. Now activate the computer and enter that number. The computer displays the pukoid's personal log. Read it, then leave the building. Walk Roger southwest to arrive at the secret area. On the ledge is a canisterPrimordial Soup which bears the Genetix logo. Look at it to find out that it is toxic. Write the co-ordinates down that  are listed, then exit the area by clicking the Walk cursor anywhere on the ledge. Return to the spot where you and Droole beamed down at, then use the communicator to beam Roger back up to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;.

Go to the bridge and sit in the captain's chair. As soon as you sit down, Flo will intercept a transmission from the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;. Quirk says that he is under attack. After the transmission ends, Flo tells Roger that the message originated somewhere near Thrakus. A second transmission appears, which show Quirk and his crew turn into pukoids. After the transmission, command Droole to Lay in a Course for Thrakus, then command him to travel at Lite Speed. When the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; has arrived at Thrakus, command Droole to travel at Regular Speed, then command him to go into Standard Orbit. Flo will tell Roger that she is detecting an escape pod beacon from the planet's surface. Press the center button on the arm of the captain's chair to summon WD40 and ask her to scan the planet. WD40 tells Roger that the atmosphere is toxic. Leave the cockpit view and go to the engineering section of the ship.

Push the red button on the east wall. This activates the elevator in the middle of the room. Stand Roger to descend into the pod bay. Open the panel on the northeast wall to get Roger an oxygen mask. Now click the Hand cursor on the control panel that sits in front of the elevator. When a set of options appear, select Elevator Door and walk into the elevator. After you go up, enter the science lab and stand on the transporter. Wear the mask and command the transporter to beam down to Thrakus.

Roger appears on one of the enormous mushrooms making up the surface. Go west to appear somewhere else on the mushroom. See that stem with the split to the right? Walk through this stem to appear at the escape pod. Just go over and look inside it. (It won't bite.) Take the frock from inside the pod and press the button on the homing device that was hidden behind the frock. This turns the device off. Exit the view by clicking outside the picture of the pod. Go west to the next screen, and then go up to the northwest corner of the mushroom. Beatrice will appear and attack Roger, mistaking him for a pukoid. Both characters roll off the side of the mushroom, and hang on to it for dear life, with Roger hanging onto the side while Beatrice hangs onto him. To make matters worse, pukoids beam down onto mushrooms below and start shooting at them with their phlegm throwers. To get out of this situation, lower the frock to Beatrice and she will climb up safely onto the mushroom.

Next, contact the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; immediately to be told that it will take a minute to re-calibrate the transporter and that he should hang on. When the communication is terminated, wait for Beatrice to throw Roger a vine. Climb up the vine. When both of them are on top of the mushrooms, more pukoids appear, and just when they start firing, both of you get beamed up onto the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;. 

Unfortunately, Beatrice is infected with Primordial Soup and you must get her into the cryogenic chamber so that she won't change rapidly. You are given the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s warp-distributor cap, and Beatrice tells Roger that the pukoids have to be stopped. When she has finished speaking to you, press the red button on the east wall to extend the cryo chamber. Open the cryo chamber, then pick her up and place her in the chamber. Now examine the cryo chamber and click the Hand cursor on the panel on the lower-left corner of the screen. You have several options, but the two you only need to worry about is Freeze and Defrost. Look at the part of the panel below the buttons, and you are instructed to freeze Beatrice for ten seconds. So enter 10 on the keypad and press the Start button. Once the ten seconds are up, Beatrice will be in cryogenic suspension. Exit the close-up view of the cryogenic chamber and return to the bridge.

Sit down in the captain's chair. Droole informs Roger that the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt; is approaching at high speed with her weapons systems armed and ready, so command Droole to Raise Shields and wait. The &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt; will make an attack pass. When Droole says that she's coming around again, command him to take Evasive Action. When you are asked what to do next, select OK! Let's risk almost certain death in the asteroid field! from the list of choices that appear. Droole will maneuver the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; into the asteroid field, avoiding the attacks. After Quirk taunts Roger, Cliffy tells Roger that he will go outside to repair the damage that the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; suffered from the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s attack. Cliffy fails as he is swept into space. As captain, you must rescue him, so stand up and return to the pod bay.

There, open the panel on the northeast wall and take an oxygen tank. Use the control panel and press the Rotate Pod to make the pod swing around and open up. Climb into the pod to leave the airlock. Save the game. Roger must find Cliffy within the asteroid field and bring him back to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; before the pod runs out of fuel or you run out of oxygen. Before you go anywhere, look at the screen at the left side, as it tells you how to pilot the pod. Once you have read that, I suggest that you try out the controls to see what they do. Once you tried each and every control that there is, proceed with your rescue mission.

Note: Computers nowadays have a problem with this sequence. When you try to move the pod left or right, the view outside the pod moves &lt;i&gt;extremely fast&lt;/i&gt;, making it almost impossible to control the pod. Setting the game at minimum speed won't work. Either buy an older computer or use &lt;a href=&quot;http://dosbox.sourceforge.net&quot;&gt;DOSBox&lt;/a&gt; to get around this.

Once the pod's mechanical arm is within Cliffy's reach, a green rectangle appears around him and a message will say that he is within range. If he is not, move up to him until he is within the arm's range. When you grab Cliffy, rotate the pod until the green blip is aligned with the vertical bar of the crosshairs. Move forward until you get back to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;. (Roger will die if he takes a long time.) 

After Cliffy gives his thanks to Roger, return to the bridge and sit in the chair. Command Droole to Lay in a Course for Genetix (the number found on the canister on Klorax II) and then command him to go to Lite Speed. When the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; is approaching Genetix, a planet in shape of a dome, order Droole to go to Regular Speed and then Standard Orbit. Stand up, go to the science lab, stand on the transporter, then command it to be beamed down to Genetix.

Just then, a fly buzzer into the transporter, and its field malfunctions, causing Roger to arrive at the surface with a body of a fly, but with his own head. Save the game here, and have a look at the icon bar to notice that some of the commands have been disabled. Fly Roger over to the east side of the pool until a mutated frog leaps out from the water and attempts to eat Roger. The frog will miss Roger and land on the communicator. When the communicator has been activated, land on it and talk to Flo. You will be told that an underground structure lies to the west. Once the communication terminates, fly Roger west to get to a waterfall.

There is also a doorway with an electronic keypad next to it. Since you don't have a keycard and can't insert one anyway, you need to fly into the keycard slot. Inside the slot, you will be faced with several beams of light protruding from the ceiling, and there is a row of lock tumblers to the right. When Roger passes through a beam, either you will hear a click and see a tumbler move, or nothing will happen at all. Only pass through all of the beams that make a sound. After you have done this, go north into the Genetix laboratory. 

Here, fly down to the computer screen next to the east wall and land on it. Land on the Restart button to restart the computer. Once it functions, land on Security to bring up a picture that has three domes in it. Walk over to dome number three and press Security. This will bring up views from security cameras one and three. Number one shows Roger's body climbing into a dumpster. Switch to camera number two, which slows the pool. Switch to number three, which slows the waterfall, as well as Cliffy and WD40 beaming down to search for Roger. Move the Fly icon off the screen and click on Fly Away to leave the view of the screen. Fly back through the lock. 

Once outside, land on Cliffy and he will ask Roger to show him where Roger's body is. After Cliffy has done talking to you, fly off behind the big rock outcropping to the east and Cliffy follows. When he opens the dumpster behind the rock, Roger's body falls out with the garbage. Cliffy instructs Roger to land on his own body so that he can try to reverse whatever it is that happened in the teleporter, so do what he says and Cliffy returns you back to normal. Now follow Cliffy back into the lab. Use the hole punch on the business card to bring a close-up view of both items. Punch holes in the same pattern as the beams that were silent (should be shaped like an X in the end). Insert the card into the slot to open the door.

Cliffy waits for you outside the lab. Turn on the computer on the east wall. Return to the main menu and click the Projects button. Read about Primordial Soup to learn that the mutations caused by the Soup are slowed down dramatically by the application of extreme cold temperatures. Return to the main menu and select Accounting. Read through the accounting file to learn that Genetix paid Quirk vast amounts of money as bribes. Return to the main menu and move the Hand cursor off the screen. Click on Exit to return to the lab. Press the black panel on the north wall to reveal to tanks of liquid nitrogen. Take both of them and leave the lab. WD40 returns from patrolling the area and gives Roger the communicator back, then Cliffy beams her up to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; and Roger gives him the liquid nitrogen. When he asks you if you want to get beamed up or stay on Genetix, tell him to beam you up.

A sequence appears where Spike tries to tell them something by jumping around between the transporter and the cryo chamber. When Roger asks for a translation, select We should initiate a manual control bypass to reverse the phase polarity of the interface grid and then use the transporter to reintegrate Beatrice's DNA molecules. from the choices that appear. While Cliffy adjusts the transporter, look at the cryo chamber and click the Hand cursor on it for a close-up. Press Defrost and enter 10 on the keypad. Hit the Start button and watch Beatrice get defrosted. Now open the cryo chamber and remove her body. Put her on the transporter and Cliffy cures her. Roger and Beatrice talk for a while, and Roger will put her back in the cryo chamber so that she can get some rest. Return to the bridge.

Sit in the captain's chair and command Droole to Lay in a Course for Gingivitis, then. command him to travel at Lite Speed. When the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt; arrives at Gingivitis, command Droole to travel at Regular Speed. You will be told that the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt; will be in visual range in ten seconds. Use the left button on the chair's arm to call Cliffy and order him to Cloak the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;. Leave the chair and return to the science lab. There, Cliffy will show Roger a hologram of the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt; and tell him that there aren't many pukoids in the engineering spaces. The hologram will highlight the central portion in orange. After Cliffy stops yakking, look at that portion and Cliffy will tell you about it. Look at the rear, then move the Eye cursor along the central part of the hull until you come to a highlighted section. This is the third panel from the rear, and it is the area where fewer pukoids are

Go down to the pod bay. Rotate the pod and climb inside to arrive outside the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;. Click the Hand cursor on the third panel from the left of the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s hull. The EVA will approach the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt; and attack itself to the area. This brings up an inside view of the rear of the pod. Press the white button to open the pod's door. Save the game, then cut a hole in the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s hull with the cutting torch. Roger will climb through the hull and find himself in the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s engine room. If the pukoids kill you, save the game.

You arrive on a staircase underneath the catwalk. Wait for the pukoid to leave the area, and go over to the computer at the end of the catwalk. Bring a close-up view of it by clicking the Hand cursor on it. What you see is the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s warp-motivator. Place the warp-distributor cap on the motivator. Click the Hand cursor outside the picture to leave the close-up. Wait for the pukoid to leave again, then go through the doorway to the north to arrive at a hallway. The floor consists of metal grates. Lift up a section of it and Roger will climb down into the vent. Save the game. The vents are made up of nine levels. Roger is on the eighth level and must make it to the second. On the right side of the screen is a direction pad with arrows. Use the keyboard or mouse to click on the arrows. 

Go north, east, and north (x2) to arrive at an elevator shaft. Climb up the ladder until the screen changes, then climb Roger into the topmost of the two sub-floor entrances you find. You will arrive at sub-level six. Here, go south, west, north (x2), east, and north (x2) to arrive at another elevator shaft. Climb the ladder to the next screen then climb into the topmost of the sub-floor entrances. Roger will arrive at level four. Go south, west, north (x2), west (x2), and north (x2) to arrive at an elevator shaft. Climb the ladder to the top and enter through the first sub-floor entrance. You will appear at level two. Go south (x2), west, south, east, and south. Click the Hand cursor on the on/off switch to bring a close-up, then click it again to turn off the shields.

Watch the cut-scene which results in WD40 busting in and freezing the pukoids with liquid nitrogen. Cliffy plans to cure the pukoids in an attempt to stop them destroying the universe. When you gain control again, save the game. When the pukoids all stand on the transporter, wait until the doors to the room are shut, then click the Command cursor on Cliffy. Using the transporter the same way he did for Beatrice, Cliffy transforms the pukoids into the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;'s crew and dump the Primordial Soup out into space. While this is all happening, Quirk takes off from the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt; in a shuttle and lands in the Soup, causing him to become a big blob. When the blob makes it move and attacks the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;, tell Flo to beam Roger back to the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;.

Return to the bridge and sit in the captain's chair. You see the blob attacking the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;. Command Droole to Fire at it. The blob turns back then attacks the &lt;i&gt;Eureka&lt;/i&gt;. As soon as this happens, command Droole to Activate RRS. This sucks the bastard up into the waste compartment. Order Flo to Abandon Ship. The crew leaves to beam over to the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;. You're on your own. Sit down again and press the far right button on the chair's arm. This brings up the arming mechanism for the self-destruct system. Activate the self-destruct mechanism and go to the science lab. You have ten minutes to escape. Get Beatrice out from inside the cryo chamber and Spike out of the tank. Now stand on the transporter and then command it. Damn, the fuse breaks.

Place Spike back in the tank then leave. The blob will have started to ooze out of the waste compartment. Climb into the maintenance tunnel in the east wall, then save the game. You will be looking at six fuses. Remove the center fuse among the bottom tree, then replace it with the fuse from the toolbox. Climb out of the maintenance tunnel to see the blob burst out in front of Roger. Enter the science lab. Roger goes over to the door and opens it, but the blob will grow a hand and force him away from it. Click the Walk cursor on the open doorway to leap into the science lab. Beatrice beams out onto the &lt;i&gt;Goliath&lt;/i&gt;. Remove Spike from the tank, stand on the transporter, and click the Command icon on it to beam out.

Game over, man.
</secrets>
  <genre>
   <line>
    <col>Adventure</col>
   </line>
  </genre>
 </item>
